Section: devel
Maintainer: Alexandre Bustico <alexandre.bustico@cena.fr>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 13), g++ (>= 4:13), pkg-config, libxt-dev, libx11-dev, tcl-dev, libglib2.0-dev, libpcre2-dev, libreadline-dev
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Standards-Version: 3.9.2
Homepage: http://www2.tls.cena.fr/products/ivy/

Package: ivy-c-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: ivy-c (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}, libc6-dev, libx11-dev, libglib2.0-dev, libpcre2-dev
Suggests: tclsh, wish
Description: Ivy software bus. development Package
 This package is needed for compiling applications using ivy-c.
 Ivy is mostly a communication convention between processes, implemented
 through libraries in several languages and for several platforms,
 from C to Perl, from Macintosh or WindowsNT to Linux or Unix.

Package: ivy-cpp
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Depends: ivy-c (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Ivy software bus - C++23 runtime libraries
 C++23 bindings for the Ivy software bus, with owned buses, scoped
 subscriptions and checked error results.
 This package contains the native and GLib shared library variants.

Package: ivy-cpp-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: ivy-cpp (= ${binary:Version}), ivy-c-dev (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Ivy software bus - C++23 development files
 Headers, static libraries, linker symlinks and pkg-config metadata for
 building C++23 applications with Ivy. Both native and GLib variants
 are included; select one variant per application.

